# This package's own ignore rules: Zig build artefacts, Nix outputs and devenv
# state, and nothing else.
#
# Upstream's own ignore file is preserved untouched at `src/.gitignore` and is
# one of the 614 digested files in UPSTREAM.sha256. Nothing in this file
# removes, narrows or reorders an upstream entry, and this file does not reach
# into src/ at all.
#
# Which upstream entries were broad enough to need a re-include: **none did.**
# Every pattern below is a fork-owned artefact name, and none of them is matched
# by anything in `src/.gitignore`. The one upstream entry that is close enough
# to be worth naming is `pnglibconf.[ch]` in upstream's libpng-configuration
# block, which would match this package's *generated* header by name anywhere a
# slash-less Git pattern applies. It matches nothing today, because the
# generator writes into the build cache and never into the tree -- that is the
# decision, and it is why no `!pnglibconf.h` re-inclusion is needed here. If a
# future wave ever generates into the tree instead, THAT is the wave that must
# add the re-inclusion, and it must not remove upstream's entry to make room.
# See FORK-NOTES.md section 10.
#
# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# See FORK-LICENSE.md for what that identifier covers.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# zig build artefacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These are directories rather than single files because a normal `zig build`
# creates them, and a normal `zig build` must not dirty the tree or leak into
# the package published from it. None of them is named in build.zig.zon
# `.paths`, so an ignored directory can never become part of the package.
.zig-cache/
zig-out/

# Zig 0.16 fetches dependencies into a project-local directory. This package
# declares one dependency, the sibling zlib, by relative path rather than by a
# URL, so nothing is fetched -- this entry exists so that a future URL-pinned
# dependency cannot commit a fetched tree into the repository.
zig-pkg/

# The consumer package builds inside this repository and has its own cache and
# output tree. It is ignored here as well as in consumer/.gitignore so a build
# run from the repository root cannot commit it by accident.
consumer/.zig-cache/
consumer/zig-out/
consumer/zig-pkg/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nix and devenv working-tree artefacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `nix build` writes `result` (and `result-1`, `result-2`, ... on a rebuild)
# into the directory that asked for it, and `devenv` writes its resolved inputs
# and its state beside the project. None of them is named in build.zig.zon
# `.paths`, so an ignored path can never become part of the package either.
#
# `devenv.lock` and `flake.lock` are deliberately *not* here: they are real
# inputs, they belong to the driver, and ignoring them would be the wrong way
# to keep a build out of a commit. Neither is present in this tree today, and
# `build.zig.zon` `.paths` names neither, because naming a path that does not
# exist would make `zig fetch` hash a missing entry.
result
result-*
.devenv/
.devenv.flake.nix
.devenv.flakes/
devenv.local.nix
.direnv/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scratch, deliberately not ignored
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The fixture generator `tools/make-fixtures.py` writes wherever it is told,
# which is `fixtures/` and those files are committed and digested. There is no
# ignore rule for generated fixtures, because there are none outside the tree,
# and adding one would be a way to lose an input to the tests without noticing.